   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## One sound for every node that listens\n\n**kubakub sound** holds the sound and how it is heard: tempo, how loud (gain), how fast a level falls (release), which\nfrequencies, how strong a hit must be (threshold). After a run it draws the sound: the orange line is the loudness,\nthe bars are the beats, the dots are the hits in the high, mid and low frequencies (bright = counts).\n\nIts `sound` output goes to the `sound` input of **kubakub shader** and **kubakub mask animate** here; height animate,\nmotion guide, shader mix and sound mask swap take it too. A node with the cable hides its own sound settings, and all\nof them step on the same beat. No audio connected = a built-in beat: connect **Load Audio** to `audio` for your music.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
